// Fact-level retraction fails OPEN on the carrying commit (SPEC.md SS7:
// "a reference naming a commit that doesn't exist, or a triple that
// commit never asserted, has no effect -- fails closed on the specific
// bad reference, fails open on the carrying commit. The rest of that
// commit's contribution is unaffected"). SPEC-DRIVEN: written and checked
// via `forge goal` before any implementation existed.
//
// The other half of the deliberate pair with
// cross_repo_consume_fails_closed.th: same SS7 passage, opposite posture,
// for a different severity of problem. A dangling fact-level reference is
// "an ordinary dangling reference" (SS7), NOT a structural violation --
// so unlike the cross-repo case, it must NEVER take down the whole
// carrying commit, no matter what.
//
// `factref_dangles` stands in for whether this one retraction's
// reference doesn't resolve to a real triple. `rest_of_commit_valid`
// stands in for whatever every other check on this commit concludes. The
// `ens` requires the result to equal `rest_of_commit_valid` UNCONDITIONALLY
// -- it must not depend on `factref_dangles` at all. An implementation
// that invalidates the whole commit when the dangling case is hit (the
// natural but WRONG mirror of the cross-repo contract's posture) cannot
// satisfy this.

fn commit_valid(factref_dangles: bool, rest_of_commit_valid: bool) -> bool
  req true
  ens result == rest_of_commit_valid
  fx  pure
{
  rest_of_commit_valid
}
